##############################################################################
# fee-split-vaults - every environment variable any package reads.
#
# THERE ARE NO REAL VALUES IN THIS FILE and there must never be. Copy it to
# .env (which .gitignore excludes) and fill it in there.
#
# Nothing here has a default that would let a process run against the wrong
# chain, the wrong factory, or with disclosure naming nobody. A missing
# required variable is a boot-time refusal, not a runtime surprise.
#
# Every variable read by apps/, packages/, ops/ or tools/ appears here. The
# converse does NOT hold, and the exceptions are marked: a handful of variables
# are the intended deployment interface for wiring that does not exist yet, and
# each says "NOT YET READ" on its own line. Nothing is listed here without
# saying which of the two it is.
#
# THE RULE FOR EVERY FLEET_* SWITCH BELOW is all-or-nothing. Leaving a switch
# unset means the in-memory fake for that dependency, recorded as a fake in
# the fleet's substitution banner and refused outright under
# FLEET_REFUSE_FAKES=1. Setting a switch and then failing to supply what it
# needs - a key, an endpoint, a mapping - is a STARTUP REFUSAL
# (FleetStartupRefused), never a quiet fall-back to the fake. A process that
# reports healthy while serving fiction is the one failure this file exists
# to make impossible, so each variable below says what its malformed value
# refuses with.
#
# History, because the corrections are the record: an audit on 2026-09-08
# found TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN documented as read when nothing read it, and
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY documented as unread. The integration wave of 2026-09-15
# inverted both: packages/fleet/src/credentials.ts reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and
# packages/adapters' Telegram inbound reads TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. That wave also
# added every FLEET_* variable, the settlement, price, evidence and publisher
# credentials, and VENUE_RPC_TIMEOUT_MS, none of which appeared here at all.
#
# docs/RUNNING-LOCALLY.md is the table form of this file: per variable, whether
# anything can derive it, whether it has a safe default, or whether a human has
# to supply it. `npm run bootstrap` writes the derivable ones for you.
##############################################################################


# =============================================================================
# CHAIN. Read by apps/api (config.ts), packages/fleet (adapters.ts) and tools/
# (lib/env.ts).
# =============================================================================

# Must equal VENUE.chainId in config/protocol.ts (4663). Any other value is
# refused at boot: a service pointed at another chain verifies signatures
# against the wrong EIP-712 domain and predicts vault addresses that do not
# exist. Optional; defaults to the protocol constant.
VENUE_CHAIN_ID=4663

# Two or more independent JSON-RPC endpoints, comma separated. Read by apps/api.
# TWO IS THE MINIMUM AND IT IS NOT NEGOTIABLE. The indexer sends every read to
# two providers and refuses unless they agree exactly. There is no
# single-provider fallback, because a lying or lagging provider is exactly the
# failure this design exists to catch. apps/api ALSO accepts the fleet's
# spelling below (VENUE_RPC_URL + VENUE_RPC_URL_SECONDARY) when this is unset,
# so one pair of variables can serve both processes.
VENUE_RPC_URLS=

# The fleet's PRIMARY endpoint (packages/fleet/src/adapters.ts), apps/api's
# primary when VENUE_RPC_URLS is unset, and the single endpoint tools/ uses.
# REQUIRED when FLEET_CHAIN=live; unset then refuses with "FLEET_CHAIN=live
# needs a chain to read".
VENUE_RPC_URL=

# The SECONDARY endpoint, the other half of the two-provider quorum, for the
# fleet and for apps/api alike. Defaults to https://rpc.ordofi.network, a named
# independent provider, and the pair is printed in each startup banner. Setting
# it EQUAL to VENUE_RPC_URL is refused: a quorum of one provider agreeing with
# itself is not a quorum. Also the second endpoint for tools/cross-verify.ts.
VENUE_RPC_URL_SECONDARY=

# Per-request timeout for the fleet's and apps/api's RPC clients. Default 20000.
VENUE_RPC_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Requests per second PER ENDPOINT for the fleet's and apps/api's chain reads.
# Default 0.8, which is what Venue was measured to answer. Zero, negative or
# non-numeric is refused ("is not a positive rate"). ALSO READ BY tools/ with a
# default of 4; if one .env serves both, know that 4 is five times the chain's
# measured rate and earned the first live run an HTTP 429. Leave it unset for
# the services.
VENUE_HTTP_RPS=

# eth_getLogs chunk size in blocks for the fleet's scans. Default 10000. Must
# be an integer: it is parsed as a BigInt and a non-integer throws at boot.
# ALSO READ BY tools/ (default 5000).
VENUE_LOG_CHUNK_BLOCKS=

# How many chunk ranges one sync may scan before it stops and reports
# `stillBehind`. Default 2. The scan is incremental and resumes from the stored
# cursor, so a small budget is a slow catch-up, not a lost one.
FLEET_MAX_RANGES_PER_SYNC=

# How far behind the head (seconds) a coin's chain coverage may lag before its
# tick refuses to act on stale movements. Default 3600.
FLEET_MAX_COVERAGE_LAG_SECONDS=


# =============================================================================
# CONTRACTS. Read by apps/api. All three come from the deployed VaultFactory.
# =============================================================================

# The VaultFactory. Also the EIP-712 `verifyingContract`, so a signature is
# bound to one factory as well as one chain.
VENUE_VAULT_FACTORY=

# factory.deployer(). THIS IS THE CREATE2 BASE ADDRESS, NOT THE FACTORY.
# VaultFactory embedding CoinVault's init code exceeded EIP-170, so it
# delegates to a VaultDeployer it constructs. Using the factory address here
# yields wrong vault addresses silently, and a wrong address means a dev points
# their fee revenue at a contract that does not exist.
VENUE_VAULT_DEPLOYER=

# factory.VAULT_INIT_CODE_HASH(). 32-byte hex.
VENUE_VAULT_INIT_CODE_HASH=


# =============================================================================
# OPERATOR IDENTITY AND DISCLOSURE.
# =============================================================================

# The legal operating entity. config/protocol.ts ships
# DISCLOSURE.operatorName = 'SET_ME_BEFORE_LAUNCH', and the publisher, the desk
# and the API all REFUSE TO CONSTRUCT while it is still a placeholder. apps/api
# reads this variable; the FLEET'S PUBLISHER DOES NOT - under FLEET_PUBLISHER=live
# it takes the name from DISCLOSURE.operatorName in config/protocol.ts and
# refuses to construct until that constant is edited to the real name. That is
# README launch gate (e), and there is no environment variable that bypasses it.
VENUE_OPERATOR_NAME=

# Public receipts base URL for apps/api. Must be https. Receipt links in every
# disclosure footer are built from it, so it is part of the compliance surface.
VENUE_RECEIPTS_BASE_URL=

# Bearer token for every non-public API route. At least 32 characters,
# compared in constant time. Rotate it like a password.
VENUE_OPERATOR_API_TOKEN=

# The published terms apps/api pins into a consent when a dev quotes through
# the web (POST /v1/onboarding/quote) and publishes at GET /v1/protocol: the
# Venue adapter the vault claims through, keccak256 of the versioned MSA, and
# where that MSA is read (https). All three together or none; unset means
# those two routes answer 503 terms_unconfigured and the operator-driven
# POST /onboarding, which carries them per request, is the only intake.
# VENUE_REFERRER_SHARE_BPS is the referrer's share of the operator slice a web
# quote naming a referrer is offered; unset means such a quote is refused.
VENUE_ADAPTER=
VENUE_TERMS_HASH=
VENUE_TERMS_URL=
VENUE_REFERRER_SHARE_BPS=

# Per-coin user_id salt for model calls, held only by the operator. ROTATING IT
# SPLITS A CLIENT'S ABUSE HISTORY INTO TWO IDENTITIES, so treat a rotation as
# an incident, not as hygiene. Read by packages/fleet/src/bootstrap.ts. Unset
# means the sandbox salt, which is derived from the coin ref and recorded in
# the banner as the `userIdSalt` fake; the fleet REFUSES to start without this
# beside ANY real dependency (a real model, chain, store or transport).
FLEET_USER_ID_SALT=

# HMAC key for the signed spend-policy token, and its key id. No model context
# can reach or forge these; the broker's keyring redacts itself on every
# serialisation path so key material cannot ride into a prompt. Read by
# packages/fleet/src/adapters.ts: both or neither (one without the other is a
# refusal), the key is at least 32 bytes, and the id must not be the sandbox's
# "policy-sandbox". Unset means the sandbox key that ships in
# packages/fleet/src/sandbox.ts, recorded in the banner as the `policyKeyring`
# MONEY PATH fake - and FLEET_SETTLEMENT=live or FLEET_CATALOG=data REFUSE to
# start beside it, because a pull or a catalog quote authorised under a key
# that ships in the source is authorised by nobody.
POLICY_SIGNING_KEY=
POLICY_SIGNING_KEY_ID=


# =============================================================================
# API SERVICE.
#
# THE API AND THE FLEET SHARE ONE SET OF VARIABLES for everything they both
# touch: DATABASE_URL (one database, so a pending purchase the runner records
# is the one the API clears), VENUE_RPC_URL / VENUE_RPC_URL_SECONDARY (one
# quorum), OPERATOR_SIGNER_KEY (one signer: it deploys vaults here and settles
# pulls there), PUBLISHER_TOKEN_KEY (one sealing key, or the fleet cannot open
# a credential the API stored), COINGECKO_IDS with FLEET_PRICES=coingecko (one
# price map), CREATIVE_FONT_FILES (one font set, or the two hosts render
# different bytes) and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Each is documented once, in its own
# section; apps/api reads the same name with the same refusal. Its startup
# banner lists which resolved to the real thing and which did not.
# =============================================================================

PORT=8080

# How stale a screening may be before activation is refused. Default 7 days.
VENUE_SCREENING_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=604800

# How long after launch before a coin may be ACTIVATED. Charging happens
# exclusively in ACTIVE, so holding activation is the whole mitigation for the
# 99%-at-t=0 anti-snipe tax: the windfall lands before we are charging.
# Default 900 (15 minutes) against a decay of roughly 3 seconds. The launch
# time comes from the TokenLaunched log on the Venue factory, scanned back from
# the finalized head; a launch older than the scan window is dated by an upper
# bound, which only ever lengthens the hold.
VENUE_ANTI_SNIPE_HOLD_SECONDS=900

# X app-only bearer token (OAuth 2.0 application-only) that lets apps/api read
# a tweet named as a narrative source through GET /2/tweets/:id. OPTIONAL and
# fails closed: unset, an x.com / twitter.com status URL among a coin's
# narrative sources is refused (x_token_missing), never scraped. Read only by
# apps/api; the publisher's posting credentials are the user-context tokens
# under X_CLIENT_ID below and are a different thing.
X_READ_BEARER_TOKEN=

# The operator's slur list for stage-1 screening, as a JSON array of
# {term, category, requireBoundary?, note?} in the parseLexiconJson shape
# (packages/screening/src/lexicon.ts). IT IS NOT CHECKED IN and never will be.
# Read by apps/api (live.ts) and the ops rescreen job. Unset: the builtin
# publishable list only, recorded as a fake, and NO CLEAR VERDICT CAN ISSUE
# (lexicon_unconfigured). Set but unreadable, empty, or naming an unknown
# category: a STARTUP REFUSAL naming the file.
SCREENING_LEXICON_FILE=

# The official OFAC SDN list, loaded once at boot into SdnScreener. Either the
# legacy sdn.csv (12 columns, no header) or sdn.xml. OFAC_SDN_FILE is a local
# copy and wins; otherwise OFAC_SDN_URL is fetched, defaulting to
# https://www.treasury.gov/ofac/downloads/sdn.csv. The list is AUTHORITATIVE -
# able to clear - only when it can be dated: sdn.xml carries Publish_Date,
# sdn.csv does not and is dated by the HTTP Last-Modified header, so a CSV
# read from a local file is loaded but not authoritative (use sdn.xml for a
# file). A list older than DEFAULT_SDN_POLICY.maxListAgeSeconds (7 days)
# raises sanctions_list_stale; restart to reload. A NAMED file or URL that
# cannot be loaded is a STARTUP REFUSAL; the unnamed default download failing
# is a recorded fake (the sample list, which cannot clear).
OFAC_SDN_URL=
OFAC_SDN_FILE=

# Only 'production' changes anything: it turns on the refusals below. Anything
# else - including unset - is treated as a laptop, a test runner or staging.
NODE_ENV=

# Written by `npm run bootstrap` (tools/bootstrap-env.ts) to mark an environment
# that contains DEV-ONLY sentinels from config/dev-only.ts. apps/api REFUSES TO
# BOOT with it set while NODE_ENV=production, and separately refuses the
# sentinel values themselves and any factory or deployer address no CREATE or
# CREATE2 could reach. Leave it unset here; the generator sets it in .env.local.
VENUE_DEV_ONLY_CONFIG=


# =============================================================================
# WEB APP (apps/web). Read by Vite at build and dev time, not at runtime.
# =============================================================================

# Base URL of apps/api. UNSET IS THE WORKING MODE TODAY: with no value the app
# runs on its in-memory fixture backend and says so in the chrome. Setting it
# switches the identical UI to HttpApiClient - but apps/web asks for /v1/*
# routes that apps/api does not serve yet, and sends no operator token, so every
# request returns 401 or 404. docs/RUNNING-LOCALLY.md has the route diff.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=


# =============================================================================
# DATABASE. Read by ops/scheduler/main.ts, ops/migrations/cli.ts, apps/api and
# the fleet's composition root (packages/fleet/src/ports.ts).
# =============================================================================

# Postgres. REQUIRED by the scheduler: there is no in-memory production mode,
# and it refuses to start with pending migrations (`node ops/migrations/cli.js
# up` first). With it set the fleet's composition root uses every durable
# store: vaults, screening, receipts, approvals, invoices, the ledger, the
# image store, the publisher's registries, the delivery-predicate queue, the
# spend counters, the escalation sink and - under FLEET_CHAIN=live - the fee
# indexer. apps/api uses the SAME database for onboarding, the publisher
# stores, images, invoices, pending purchases, receipts, the ledger and the
# agent-run reads; without it the API's stores are in-memory and its
# purchases, creative and /accounts/x routes answer 503. Without it
# (tools/fleet.ts, a one-off run) the fleet's stores are in-memory and do not
# survive a restart. FLEET_COINS_SOURCE=db and TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN both REFUSE
# without it, by name.
DATABASE_URL=


# =============================================================================
# FLEET: THE MODEL. Read by packages/fleet/src/credentials.ts.
# =============================================================================

# Anthropic API key for the reader, planner, desk and screening adjudicator.
# READ, as of 2026-09-15: credentials.ts passes it to the SDK explicitly, and
# with it unset lets the SDK try its own resolution. If no client can be built
# the fleet runs the SCRIPTED model and records provenance 'fake' - visible in
# the banner and in every agent-run record, and a refusal under
# FLEET_REFUSE_FAKES=1. T0 is deterministic by design and needs no key; every
# paid tier does. apps/api reads it for narrative derivation and NEVER runs
# scripted: unset, or set but not confirmed live, the derive route answers 503.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# '0' skips the one-token probe that confirms the credential at startup. The
# run then reports provenance 'live' on the operator's say-so, and the banner
# says so. Any other value probes.
FLEET_MODEL_PROBE=

# '1' turns a probe that failed for a NON-auth reason (network, 5xx) into a
# refusal (ModelCredentialUnresolved) instead of a scripted run. An auth
# failure is always a scripted run with provenance 'fake', never 'live'.
FLEET_REQUIRE_LIVE_MODEL=

# '1' refuses to start if ANY dependency resolved to a fake - model, chain,
# settlement, prices, evidence, publisher, message source, stores - and names
# every one of them in the refusal. THIS IS THE PRODUCTION SETTING. Leave it
# unset only on a laptop where a fake is what you want.
FLEET_REFUSE_FAKES=


# =============================================================================
# FLEET: THE CHAIN. Read by packages/fleet/src/adapters.ts. The endpoint and
# rate variables are in the CHAIN section above.
# =============================================================================

# 'live' reads Venue over the two-provider quorum (VENUE_RPC_URL plus
# VENUE_RPC_URL_SECONDARY) and tracks each coin's vault from its deployment
# block; a coin whose directory row names no deployment block is refused, not
# scanned from 0 and not started at the head. Unset means the fixture chain.
# ANY OTHER VALUE is refused: "is not a mode this build knows".
FLEET_CHAIN=

# 'index' replays every bound memecoin's ERC-20 Transfer log into Postgres
# token_holder_balance (packages/indexer/src/holders.ts), to the FINALIZED
# head, one cursor per token, and builds the REAL qualification signals from
# it: unique buyers and self-trade share from the indexed curve trades, top-10
# and deployer share from the holder table (the curve, vault, locker, buyback
# vault, hook and the hook's poolManager() are custodians, not holders), and
# Venue-pool volume share from the fee postings against Dexscreener's 24h
# volume (FLEET_EVIDENCE=dexscreener; without it a post-graduation coin's
# signals REFUSE). Needs FLEET_CHAIN=live, DATABASE_URL and
# FLEET_PRICES=coingecko. Unset on a live chain means the signals are the
# sandbox's fixed numbers, and the banner lists `signals` as a MONEY PATH fake.
FLEET_HOLDERS=

# The chain sync runs inside every tick's prepare step on a live chain (one
# scan per instant, shared by every coin ticking at it). A coin whose vault
# scan or the fleet's fee scan is still behind the head with a coverage
# watermark older than FLEET_MAX_COVERAGE_LAG_SECONDS (CHAIN section above)
# has its tick REFUSED (FleetTickRefused) rather than answered from blocks
# nobody read.

# Where the coin directory comes from. 'db' reads onboarding rows in state
# `active` from the onboarding table (written by apps/api), with publisher
# bindings and image assets alongside, and refuses without DATABASE_URL.
# 'file' reads the JSON named by FLEET_COINS_FILE and refuses without it.
# Unset means 'file' when FLEET_COINS_FILE is set, else the fixture fleet -
# and the fixture fleet under FLEET_CHAIN=live is refused ("would scan the
# chain for fixture coins that do not exist there"). Any other value is
# refused: "is not a source this build knows".
FLEET_COINS_SOURCE=

# Path to a coin-directory JSON, used when FLEET_COINS_SOURCE=file (and, for
# tools/fleet.ts, whenever it is set at all). A file that does not parse as a
# coin directory is refused with the offending field.
FLEET_COINS_FILE=


# =============================================================================
# FLEET: SETTLEMENT. The one dependency that can move money.
# =============================================================================

# 'live' constructs ChainSettlementPort (packages/adapters/src/chain/settlement.ts):
# every reimbursement pull becomes a CoinVault.pullBudget transaction signed by
# the operator key, simulated first, confirmed to depth, and refused before
# any RPC if its destination is not OPERATOR_TREASURY_ADDRESS. Unset means the
# fake settlement port, which records pulls and moves nothing. Requires
# FLEET_CHAIN=live (there is no chain to broadcast on otherwise) and BOTH
# variables below; any of the three missing is a refusal.
FLEET_SETTLEMENT=

# The operator's signing key: 0x followed by 64 hex characters. Wrong length,
# zero, or at/above the curve order is refused at construction. THIS IS THE
# ONLY SECRET THAT CAN MOVE FUNDS. It reaches the orchestrator container from
# a secrets manager at runtime; never through a build argument, never in an
# image, never in this file. apps/api reads the same key to sign
# VaultFactory.deploy; without it every vault deployment REFUSES.
OPERATOR_SIGNER_KEY=

# The operator treasury: the ONLY address a pull may pay. Rule 3 of the broker
# is re-asserted here on every submit ("destination_not_treasury"), so even a
# broker bug cannot point a client's budget at a vendor. Must be a 20-byte
# address, not the zero address, and NOT the address OPERATOR_SIGNER_KEY
# derives: a leaked hot signer must not be a leaked treasury. Each is refused
# by name.
OPERATOR_TREASURY_ADDRESS=


# =============================================================================
# FLEET: PRICES AND DELIVERY EVIDENCE.
# =============================================================================

# 'coingecko' prices quote assets from CoinGecko's /simple/price, cached 60s,
# refusing undated quotes, quotes older than the broker's freshness window,
# sub-cent quotes and unmapped assets - a refused price pins nothing, so QF
# cannot be measured, no tier granted, no spend authorised. Unset means the
# fixture price book. Requires COINGECKO_IDS. apps/api reads the same switch
# for the weekly report's USD figures; at boot it describes every mapped asset
# from its own contract (decimals, symbol) and refuses to start if it cannot.
FLEET_PRICES=

# JSON object mapping quote-asset ADDRESS to CoinGecko id, e.g.
# {"0x5fc5360d0400a0fd4f2af552add042d716f1d168":"global-dollar"}. A key that is
# not an address, or an empty id, is refused at construction.
COINGECKO_IDS=

# Optional. Sent as x-cg-demo-api-key (or x-cg-pro-api-key against the pro
# origin). Unset uses the public rate limit.
COINGECKO_API_KEY=

# 'dexscreener' verifies eti_listing and boost_delta predicates against
# Dexscreener's token-pairs API; trending_rank, kol_post and manual_attestation
# are reported unmeasurable by it and fail closed. Unset means the fake
# evidence source. Requires DEXSCREENER_CHAIN_SLUG.
FLEET_EVIDENCE=

# Dexscreener's path segment for Venue. THERE IS NO DEFAULT: the operator
# confirms it against Dexscreener's chain list, and an empty value refuses.
DEXSCREENER_CHAIN_SLUG=

# 'data' loads the vendor and SKU catalog from data/ via loadCatalog and
# bridges it into the broker's catalog; a pass-through entry that is enabled
# without a rate card is refused ("enabled_without_rate_card"). Unset means
# the fixture catalog.
FLEET_CATALOG=

# Overrides where vendor, SKU, rate-card and screening seed data is read from.
# Defaults to the data/ directory next to packages/catalog.
VENUE_DATA_DIR=


# =============================================================================
# FLEET: MESSAGES AND PUBLISHING.
# =============================================================================

# Telegram Bot API token. READ, as of 2026-09-15, by the fleet
# (packages/fleet/src/adapters.ts -> packages/adapters' BotApiTelegramInbound).
# Set, each coin that names a telegram account gets its chat as its message
# source, stored durably because getUpdates is a consuming stream - so it
# REFUSES without DATABASE_URL, and refuses when no coin names a telegram
# account ("a bot with nothing to listen to is misconfiguration"). Unset, the
# message source is the in-memory fake and the reader sees synthetic
# messages, which the banner says. Also REQUIRED under FLEET_PUBLISHER=live.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# 'live' constructs the real X and Telegram publisher transports and the
# Postgres-backed account bindings, and passes `transportsAreReal=true` to the
# fake-authored-real-send assertion. It ALSO takes the operator name from
# DISCLOSURE.operatorName in config/protocol.ts and refuses to construct while
# that is 'SET_ME_BEFORE_LAUNCH' - edit the constant, there is no override.
# Unset means fake transports and nothing is ever sent.
FLEET_PUBLISHER=

# X (Twitter) OAuth 2.0 client for the operator account and for delegated
# client accounts. Read by apps/api (config.ts, the account-linking routes)
# and by the fleet under FLEET_PUBLISHER=live, which requires X_CLIENT_ID and
# X_REDIRECT_URI and treats X_CLIENT_SECRET as optional. In apps/api the
# three go together: X_CLIENT_ID without X_REDIRECT_URI, or the reverse, is
# refused; X_CLIENT_SECRET alone is refused; the redirect must be https.
# Either process refuses with the name of the missing one.
X_CLIENT_ID=
X_CLIENT_SECRET=
X_REDIRECT_URI=

# 32 bytes of hex (0x optional) that seals stored OAuth tokens at rest.
# REQUIRED whenever X_CLIENT_ID is set: "OAuth tokens are never stored
# unencrypted". Any other length is refused ("must be 32 bytes of hex").
PUBLISHER_TOKEN_KEY=

# Public receipts base URL the publisher builds disclosure-footer links from.
# Must be https, like VENUE_RECEIPTS_BASE_URL (the API's copy of the same
# value); set them to the same origin.
PUBLISHER_RECEIPTS_BASE_URL=

# Comma-separated hostnames a published post may link to, lowercased. Any link
# to a host not on this list is a hard reject, not a strip. Empty under
# FLEET_PUBLISHER=live is not a refusal: only the receipts host (from
# PUBLISHER_RECEIPTS_BASE_URL, which is required) may then be linked.
PUBLISHER_ALLOWED_LINK_HOSTS=

# The human review queue for posts that need approval. OPTIONAL, and absent
# FAILS CLOSED: the fleet installs the deny-all approval gate, so every post
# that needs a human is refused rather than assumed approved, and the banner
# says DENY-ALL. Set, it must be https and PUBLISHER_APPROVAL_TOKEN must be
# set with it; either is refused by name.
PUBLISHER_APPROVAL_URL=
PUBLISHER_APPROVAL_TOKEN=

# Operator-owned chat the publisher forwards its own posts into so it can read
# them back. The Bot API has no getMessage, so without this a telegram post
# cannot be re-read, and a channel we cannot re-read is one where we cannot
# prove disclosure - so the publisher DELETES the post instead.
# NOT YET READ BY ANY CODE.
TELEGRAM_AUDIT_CHAT_ID=

# The OAuth 1.0a shape of the X credentials. NOT YET READ BY ANY CODE: the
# transports built under FLEET_PUBLISHER=live use the OAuth 2.0 client above.
# Kept until docs/RUNNING-LOCALLY.md stops naming them.
X_API_KEY=
X_API_SECRET=
X_ACCESS_TOKEN=
X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=


# =============================================================================
# CREATIVE (packages/creative).
# =============================================================================

# Comma-separated .ttf paths to load INSTEAD OF relying on the host's fonts.
# Rendered asset hashes are stable per font set: with system fonts they are
# stable per host, with pinned files they are stable everywhere. The container
# images install ttf-dejavu so a render never fails `font_unresolved`; pin
# files here when two hosts must agree byte for byte. Read by apps/api, which
# renders a coin's banner, avatar and card when a narrative is approved and on
# POST /onboarding/:id/creative/render. tools/creative.ts takes --font.
CREATIVE_FONT_FILES=


# =============================================================================
# OPS SCHEDULER (ops/).
# =============================================================================

# Module path providing the real adapter ports. REQUIRED unless
# OPS_ALLOW_FAKE_PORTS=1. The composition root is @fee-split-vaults/fleet/ports, and
# it is what docker-compose.yml runs.
OPS_PORTS_MODULE=

# '1' runs the scheduler against in-memory fakes. DEVELOPMENT ONLY, and never
# together with OPS_PORTS_MODULE: it bypasses the module entirely and reports
# healthy while doing nothing.
OPS_ALLOW_FAKE_PORTS=

# Defaults to hostname:pid. Set explicitly in a container so lease ownership
# survives a restart with a new pid.
OPS_WORKER_ID=

# The LONGEST the loop sleeps between ticks, default 30. The scheduler wakes
# earlier when a fleet coin's team is due sooner (min 1s between ticks), so
# this bounds the latency of the non-fleet jobs, not the coins'. Must be a
# number >= 1; anything else is a startup refusal.
OPS_TICK_SECONDS=30
OPS_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Where a fired alert is POSTed as JSON (packages/fleet/src/ports.ts ->
# ops/scheduler/adapters/alerts.ts). https only; anything else is a startup
# refusal. Unset means ops.alerts and ops.monitoring stay the recorded fakes:
# firings are neither logged to ops_alert_firing nor paged. Optional bearer
# token for the relay in OPS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN.
OPS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
OPS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# Bot token the weekly dev report is sent with (ops.reportDelivery). Falls back
# to TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN when unset; with neither, report delivery is a recorded
# fake. The chat is the coin's bound `telegram` account in the coin directory;
# a coin without one refuses with chat_unbound. PUBLISHER_RECEIPTS_BASE_URL is
# also required: every report carries the disclosure block with a receipts link.
OPS_REPORT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# The re-screening engine (ops.screening) reads the SAME screening inputs as
# apps/api: SCREENING_LEXICON_FILE, OFAC_SDN_FILE / OFAC_SDN_URL (documented in
# the API section) and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for the adjudicator. OPERATOR_SIGNER_KEY
# (settlement section) is what the sweeper, settlement, enforcement and
# heartbeat ports sign with; without it those four stay recorded fakes.


# =============================================================================
# MEASUREMENT TOOLS (tools/). Not used by the service.
#
# NOTE: every market measurement these produced was taken INSIDE A GAS SUBSIDY
# THAT EXPIRES 29 SEPTEMBER 2026. Re-run them in October before any build
# decision. See the STATUS section of README.md.
# =============================================================================

# 'rpc' (default) or 'bitquery'.
ESCROW_BACKEND=rpc

BITQUERY_URL=
BITQUERY_TOKEN=
BITQUERY_NETWORK=

GECKOTERMINAL_BASE=
GECKOTERMINAL_NETWORK=
GECKOTERMINAL_DEX_IDS=

VENUE_CACHE_DIR=.cache/venue-tools
# VENUE_HTTP_RPS and VENUE_LOG_CHUNK_BLOCKS are in the CHAIN section: the fleet
# reads them too, with different defaults, and one value serves both.
VENUE_HTTP_MAX_RETRIES=5
VENUE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# The one-off analysis scripts in tools/artifacts/ take their input and output
# paths from the environment rather than from flags: they are the record of a
# specific investigation, not general CLIs. Each defaults to a filename beside
# the script. VENUE_RPC_BATCH sizes their JSON-RPC batches (default 10).
VENUE_ASSETS_FILE=
VENUE_COINS_OUT=
VENUE_OUT=
OUT=
CENSUS_OUT=
VENUE_RPC_BATCH=

# Approximate V2 deployment time. A MEASURED ASSUMPTION, not a read constant:
# it is the ceiling on every tenure number the tools can produce.
VENUE_V2_GENESIS_UNIX=

# L2 batch cadence drifts, so this is used ONLY to size a --dry-run request
# budget. Timestamp-to-block always goes through a binary search on headers.
VENUE_BLOCK_TIME_SECONDS=0.25

# Pinned USD prices by quote-asset symbol, e.g. VENUE_PRICE_USD_USDG=1.00.
# A missing price is a REFUSAL everywhere it matters: QF cannot be measured,
# no tier can be granted, and no spend can be authorised.
#
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_ETH PRICES THE NATIVE ASSET, and the native asset is the bulk
# of this escrow's value: the Credited event carries its amount in msg.value and
# names no token, so those credits key by address(0), symbol ETH. Without this
# variable every native recipient reports UNPRICED.
#
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_WETH is accepted as a DOCUMENTED FALLBACK for ETH when
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_ETH is unset, and every run that uses it says so in its
# warnings. They are not the same asset - WETH is a wrapper that can depeg -
# so set the ETH one for anything that gets quoted.
#
# DO NOT COPY THE 3200 BELOW. It is the shape of the variable, not a rate. The
# 7-day measurement was taken at a hand-pinned $3,200/ETH that nobody checked;
# the verified price for that window was $2,460 (ETH-weighted), which overstated
# the native total by 30% and moved the T1 standing population from 99 to 80.
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_ETH=<the verified rate, with its source recorded below>
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_WETH=<same, if you price WETH separately>
# VENUE_PRICE_USD_USDG=
#
# Free-text provenance for the prices above: name the venue and the timestamp.
# It is copied verbatim into every artifact, so "3200" with no source becomes an
# unanswerable question six months later.
VENUE_PRICE_SOURCE=


# =============================================================================
# ON-CHAIN PRICE SOURCE (tools/). OPTIONAL, and OFF unless a pool is named.
#
# Chain 4663 carries a WETH/USDG Uniswap-V3-shaped pool deep enough to quote
# from, which lets the toolkit stop depending entirely on a hand-entered number.
# Reading it is a TWAP over observe(), never slot0 spot, because spot is
# manipulable inside a single block.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT: it prices WETH rather than native ETH, and it prices in USDG
# rather than dollars, so converting assumes the USDG peg. Both caveats ride in
# the provenance string and in every run's warnings. It is a cross-check and a
# documented fallback, not an authority.
#
# PRECEDENCE: if VENUE_PRICE_USD_ETH is set, THE PINNED VALUE STILL WINS and the
# on-chain reading is reported beside it with the discrepancy. If it is unset,
# the on-chain reading fills the gap. Either way the run says which happened.
# =============================================================================

# The pool to read. No default: a price source nobody chose is one nobody
# checked. Setting this is what turns the feature on.
# The WETH/USDG 100bps pool on chain 4663, verified 2026-09-07 (6,038 WETH and
# 16.85M USDG in the pool, 30-minute TWAP $2,490 against $2,489 off-chain):
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_POOL=0x52e65b17fb6e5ba00ed806f37afcd2daa50271ca

# The stablecoin the pool quotes in, and its decimals. DECIMALS ARE REQUIRED and
# are never assumed: USDG is 6, and assuming 18 is a 10^12 error - the same one
# that rendered $9.03M of USDG as 9.033e-6.
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_QUOTE=0x5fc5360d0400a0fd4f2af552add042d716f1d168
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_QUOTE_SYMBOL=USDG
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_QUOTE_DECIMALS=6

# The peg ASSUMED for the quote asset when converting to USD. Defaults to 1.00.
# If USDG is off its peg, every USD figure derived from this price is off by the
# same factor, and the run says so.
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_QUOTE_PEG_USD=1.00

# TWAP window, seconds. Defaults to 1800. A pool whose observation cardinality
# does not cover the window REFUSES rather than falling back to spot.
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_TWAP_SECONDS=1800

# The asset being priced. Defaults to VENUE.contracts.weth from config/protocol.ts.
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_BASE=
# VENUE_ONCHAIN_PRICE_BASE_SYMBOL=WETH

# --- Desk and X mentions (DeskAndMentions) ---------------------------------
# Seconds between polls of GET /2/users/:id/mentions for every X account bound
# to a coin. Read by packages/fleet (XMentionsMessageSource.poll). Default 120.
# The desk itself needs no extra variable: TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (moderation and
# the admin-rights check), ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (the T1 desk model) and
# DATABASE_URL (PgRefusalLog) are documented in their own sections.
X_MENTIONS_POLL_SECONDS=120
